---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Chips from '../components/Chips.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import CaseStudies from '../components/CaseStudies.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'A practice can feel too small for a product studio.',
    a: 'Small is exactly who this work is for. Solo practitioners, wellness practices, small nonprofits, and community clinics in behavioral and mental health are the heart of the studio — and a wonderful place to begin.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Care Practice Studio a web agency?',
    a: 'No — and that distinction is a strength. Care Practice Studio is technical product management. Peter plans and builds custom digital products with care, rather than running a generic web shop.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does the studio serve hospital systems?',
    a: 'No. Large hospital-affiliated systems sit outside this focus, so care and attention stay with smaller, mission-driven teams.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does the work place a practice on a directory?',
    a: 'No. Directory and lead-gen sites are a different business. The aim is a product made for one team, not a public listing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does the studio already hold deep compliance credentials?',
    a: 'No. That experience is not claimed here. When a product needs a compliance review, the right reviewer belongs alongside the build — Peter will gladly work with that reviewer and will not pretend to fill that role.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Who I help"
  current="help"
  description="Care Practice Studio works one-on-one with solo practitioners, small nonprofits, and community clinics in behavioral and mental health."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow eyebrow--lg">Who I help</div>
    <h1 class="h1">Made for small practices, not hospital systems</h1>
    <p class="lede lede--italic">You care for people in rooms that stay close. This work is built for that.</p>
    <Chips />
  </section>

  <section class="section section--mint split">
    <h2 class="h2">The tools close at hand were not shaped for small practices</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Care Practice Studio works alongside solo practitioners, small nonprofits, and community clinics. Days in this work are
        already full. A modest, real-world budget can still support a clear mission.
      </p>
      <p>
        Big hospital systems already have vendors built for them. Directory sites mostly want another name on a list. Generic web
        shops tend to hand everyone the same site.
      </p>
      <p>That still leaves room for behavioral health, mental health, and a wellness practice that stays small on purpose.</p>
      <p class="emph">Those providers do not need a lead list. What fits is a product shaped around how people are actually helped.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--roomy split">
    <div class="stack" style="gap: 20px">
      <h2 class="h2">One client. One custom product.</h2>
      <p class="body-lg">
        Care Practice Studio is a solo consultancy, and that focus is a gift. Peter plans and builds custom digital products with
        real care for behavioral and mental health providers, wellness practices, solo practitioners, small nonprofits, and
        community clinics.
      </p>
      <p class="body-lg">
        Each job is one-on-one. One client at a time, so the work gets his full attention — closer and more personal than a large
        hospital-affiliated system, and nothing like a directory or lead-gen site.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="stack" style="gap: 16px">
      <ol class="numbered-cards">
        <li><span class="num">1</span><span class="txt">A practice brings the work of daily care.</span></li>
        <li><span class="num">2</span><span class="txt">Peter plans a product made only for that client.</span></li>
        <li><span class="num">3</span><span class="txt">He builds that product alongside the client, start to finish.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="kicker">No shared queue. No template pulled from a catalog.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--roomy stack" style="padding-top: 0; gap: 40px">
    <h2 class="h2">What that means for this kind of work</h2>
    <div class="two-up">
      <article class="mint-card">
        <h3 class="h3">Clients remain the focus, not a segment</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The niche is named on purpose, and it is a hopeful one: behavioral and mental health, wellness practices, solo
            practitioners, small nonprofits, and community clinics.
          </li>
          <li>Community outpatient clinics are warmly welcome. Large hospital-affiliated systems sit outside that circle.</li>
          <li>The working relationship is with Peter, a steady partner, rather than a rotating team.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="mint-card">
        <h3 class="h3">The offering is a product, not a listing</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Care Practice Studio is neither a directory nor a lead-gen site.</li>
          <li>Each build is bespoke: planned with care for one mission-driven provider.</li>
          <li>A logo on a generic healthcare package would miss the point.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CaseStudies />

  <section class="section section--roomy split" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <h2 id="faq-title" class="h2">Straight answers before the work begins</h2>
    <div class="stack">
      {
        faqs.map((f) => (
          <div class="faq__item">
            <h3>{f.q}</h3>
            <p>{f.a}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand title="When a practice fits this page" wide>
    Care Practice Studio works with one client at a time, so a small practice receives real attention. The studio is glad to support
    mission-driven behavioral and mental health providers — wellness practices, solo practitioners, small nonprofits, and community
    clinics — whose care is rooted in the community rather than in large hospital-affiliated systems or in directory and lead-gen
    sites.
  </CtaBand>
</Base>
